BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:JOIN US FOR THE LAUNCH OF EBOLA\, BOMBS\, AND MIGRANTS BY DR JOANN
 E LIU
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261130T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261130T200000
UID:bm-6681920261130@flyingbooks.ca
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/8102716/0_1.png?c
 b=1794491036
DESCRIPTION:[Book Launch]\nDr. Joanne Liu presents the new release of\nEbo
 la\, Bombs\, and\nMigrants: Humanitarian Crises in a Security-Obsessed Wor
 ld\nin partnership with House of Anansi Press and Flying Books. Dr. Liu wi
 ll be joined in a fireside chat discussion with\nNew York Times\nbestselli
 ng\nauthor\, award-winning journalist\, and filmmaker Michelle Shephard\, 
 with an opportunity\nfor audience Q&A to follow.  The book will be avail
 able for sale with an opportunity to have\nthe book signed by Dr. Liu.\nJo
 in us for an incisive view with Dr. Joanne Liu\, former International\nPre
 sident of Médecins Sans Frontières (MSF) / Doctors Without Borders who w
 ill\ndiscuss her new book\nE\nbola\, Bombs\, and Migrants: Humanitarian Cr
 ises in a Security-\nObsessed World.\nDr. Liu details her frontline experi
 ence of three major humanitarian\ncrises during her tenure and reveals gro
 wing concerns in national security and its\ncapacity to overshadow our res
 ponsibility to protect vulnerable populations.\nJOANNE LIU has spent most 
 of the last thirty years working for Médecins Sans Frontières/Doctors Wi
 thout Borders\, where she also held term as international president. In 20
 15\, Liu was made an Officer of the Ordre national du Québec and was reco
 gnized by Time Magazine as one of the 100 Most Influential People of that 
 year. She is a recipient of several recognitions\, the Légion d'honneur o
 f the French Republic\, and the Pan American Health Organization (PAHO) Aw
 ard for Health Services Management and Leadership (2021)\, and the Meritor
 ious Service Cross of Canada.
LOCATION:Flying Books\, 784 College Street
URL:https://flyingbooks.ca/events
X-SOURCE:Flying Books
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:JOIN US FOR OUR DECEMBER FICTION BOOK CLUB
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261214T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261215T203000
UID:bm-6772920261214@flyingbooks.ca
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/8102716/NOVEMBER_
 BOOK_CLUB_2026.jpg?cb=1794438506
DESCRIPTION:[Book Club]\nJoin us for a lively discussion of\nWild West\n\,
 \nMark Anthony Jarman’s wildly inventive novel set against the chaos and
  violence that swirled from Assiniboia to Montana in the late 1800s.\nOur 
 unnamed narrator has simpler things on his mind: a decent meal\, a pair of
  boots\, and the attention of a shy woman. But after stumbling upon the bo
 tched execution of Thomas Scott on Louis Riel’s orders\, he finds himsel
 f swept into the violence\, rivalries\, and competing ambitions shaping th
 e world around him.\nWild West\nrips the past out of the past and pushes i
 t right in our faces. Brutality and encroaching madness pulse through ever
 y sentence. Jarman gives us the unsettling unconscious of a chaotic new te
 rritory in a startling new light.\nJoin us on Monday\, December 14th and T
 uesday\, December 15th for an evening of  conversation. We hope to see you
  there.\nYour book club ticket includes:\nA glass of wine (or another beve
 rage of your choice).\nA thoughtful conversation with our brilliant modera
 tor\, Lee Suksi.\nA $20 credit toward any book in the shop.*\nGET YOUR TIC
 KETS HERE!\nA few details:\nTicket price includes HST and fees.\n*$20 book
  credit is valid on the night of attendance only (non-refundable and non-t
 ransferable).\nWine is served on the night of the event (ID required).\nTi
 ckets are non-refundable within 7 days of the event\; due to limited capac
 ity and planning\, we’re not able to transfer tickets to future book clu
 b sessions.
LOCATION:Flying Books at Neverland\, 371 Queen St. W.
URL:https://flyingbooks.ca/events
X-SOURCE:Flying Books
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:MAKE IT MAKE SENSE: THE FLYING BOOKS NONFICTION BOOKCLUB
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270126T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270126T203000
UID:bm-6875820270126@flyingbooks.ca
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/8102716/Jan_Nonfi
 c_2027.jpg?cb=1795715744
DESCRIPTION:[Book Club]\nFrom the winner of the Nobel Prize in Literarture
  2026\, Anne Carson's\nEros the Bittersweet\nexplores the concept of "eros
 " in both classical philosophy and literature. Beginning with\, "It was Sa
 ppho who first called eros 'bittersweet.' No one who has been in love disp
 utes her\," Carson examines her subject from numerous points of view\, cre
 ating a lyrical meditation in the tradition of William Carlos Williams's\n
 Spring and All\nand William H. Gass's\nOn Being Blue\n. An epigrammatic\, 
 witty\, ironic\, and endlessly entertaining book about romantic love.\nJoi
 n Tomas Hachard\, author of\nCity in Flames\n\, on Tuesday\, January 26th\
 , from 6:30 to 8:30 pm for an evening of conversation. We hope to see you 
 there.\nGET YOUR TICKETS HERE!\nYour book club ticket includes:\nA glass o
 f wine (or another beverage of your choice).\nA thoughtful conversation wi
 th Tomas Hachard\, author of\nCity in Flames\n.\nA $20 credit toward any b
 ook in the shop.\nA few details:\nTicket price includes HST and fees.\n$20
  book credit is valid on the night of attendance only (non-refundable and 
 non-transferable).\nWine is served on the night of the event (ID required)
 .\nTickets are non-refundable within 7 days of the event\; due to limited 
 capacity and planning\, we’re not able to transfer tickets to future boo
 k club sessions.
LOCATION:Flying Books at Neverland\, 371 Queen St. W.
URL:https://flyingbooks.ca/events
X-SOURCE:Flying Books
